# 🐞 bug report

### Affected Package
The issue is related to angular ivy compiler

### Is this a regression?
Yes, the exact use case works without issues in Angular 8.0.x (without ivy).

### Description
Given a normal angular component which references its own type in component metadata, and it's also decorated with an additional class decorator:
```
import { Component, InjectionToken, Input } from "@angular/core";

const BOUND_COMPONENT = new InjectionToken<any>("BoundComponent");

export function Bind() {
  return function(target: any) {
    console.log("Bound", target);
  };
}

@Bind()
@Component({
  selector: "hello",
  template: `
    <h1>Hello {{ name }}!</h1>
  `,
  providers: [{ provide: BOUND_COMPONENT, useExisting: HelloComponent }],
  styles: [
    `
      h1 {
        font-family: Lato;
      }
    `
  ]
})
export class HelloComponent {
  @Input() name: string;
}

will give an runtime error as you can see in stackblitz
```


